      "notes": "Closed score without any part labels: the converter must infer S/A from stem direction on the treble staff (stem up = Soprano, stem down = Alto) and T/B on the bass staff, even where the voices cross (m.3 beat 3 and m.10 the alto is ABOVE the soprano; m.12 the tenor is BELOW the bass). Unisons: shared note heads with two stems (mm.4, 10, 14, and T+B in m.7) belong to BOTH parts; in m.6 beat 3 the alto unison is drawn with one head and only the soprano's up-stem (the alto still sings a' there - the down-stem was omitted); in m.13 the soprano half note and the alto quarter on the same pitch are two separate heads. Alto rests on m.7 beat 3. Both verses are printed under the treble staff and are aligned to the soprano; truth carries them on the Soprano part only (the other parts sing the same words but the score does not print them for them). Pickup bar is measure 0."
    },
